{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for Counter contracts revision2 exactc2a938830df4534589af7f9c32d294a381b20c8c, sole primary32416b50.\n\nF2 follow-up P2 — the alarm also needs a read-authority or dormant-state contract (sections5 and7.2). The new persistent alarm fixes the lost wake while a paused team's existing agent key remains usable. But streams/sessions are renewed under an agent key, and retirement destroys those seeds. The draft says the alarm still reads both heads with zero live rows, including before first enrollment and after retire-all/restart. Internal RPC does not grant that read authority: ScopeObject.summary(reader) at object.ts458 invokes Reads authorization; Reads at reads.ts108–129 refuses a reader presenting neither an accepted session nor a qualifying signed read. sessions.ts58 documents the same. observe() at namespace.ts197 answers only native membership/rules observations, not a team/Counter head. Specify an authorized bounded read path, or a no-key dormant state explicitly resumed through the already required signed attach/enrol route. Do not keep retired signing seeds or add an unauthenticated read bypass silently. Witness initial zero-row attachment, retire-all with seed destruction and eviction, then fresh allocation/enrollment; work resumes without a browser. Keep pause-all/evict/generic-MCP resume covered while custody is available.\n\nF4 P2 — enforce the one-byte utterance minimum in the declared definition (section3; slice1). The new definition is specified as exactly fulfill's fields/guards/resolution-plan plus required utterance and recording it. Existing native text validation checks well-formedness and maximum UTF-8 bytes only (derive/src/values.ts41); required means present, not nonempty. An independent direct probe returned true for isValue({type:\"text\",max:1024,required:true},\"\",PROPOSED_BOUNDS). resolution-plan checks generation/serial/n, not utterance. Removing $contains therefore removes the implicit empty-text rejection without replacing it. Add a supported nonempty guard/rule and share that exact minimum/maximum semantics with the host. The empty-string refusal witness is already listed and must pass through real native judgment, including a generic direct say submission.\n\nAccepted responses: F1's checked integer n plus separately displayed free text is a coherent native representation: no number is inferred from text, and 13/x3x are intentionally ordinary text. F4 concerns only its remaining stated bounds. F3 is resolved at the design boundary: each selectable model now needs a justified complete input/output bound, exact wire/usage mapping and a real-binding admission test, with unsupported entries unavailable. Missing/malformed/above-limit usage retains at least the reservation, preserves larger computable cost and fences the model. A corpus alone is not a mathematical bound; the separately required tokenizer/template argument must do that work. Local versus provider cancellation/overlap, prospective budget reductions, provisional reservation-to-promise binding, and full incarnation/affiliation/control-envelope checks are now explicit.\n\nArchitecture — separate team settings and one custody/ledger/assignment object remain appropriate. The persistent control alarm is the right recovery mechanism when readable; F2 identifies its missing authority transition. Retain the named implementation slice witnesses before Source, rather than treating design review as their execution.\n\nSecurity — exact attachment ScopeRefs, directory application affiliation, live control grants, bound signed envelopes, no model tool/signing route, and per-model admission are sound boundaries. F2 must preserve read authorization; F4 must preserve native/host validation equivalence. Spending/status access by configure or administer remains consistent with the admin-only initial policy.\n\nSimplification — use an explicit dormant state or the narrowest justified read mechanism rather than adding an extra signing identity. One native nonempty check suffices for F4. Keep integer n and free text separate, and leave model-specific proof and mapping in catalog entries.\n\nAnswer to the 512-token planning question: it is acceptable as a clearly conditional arithmetic example, not a verified universal cap or an admitted reservation schedule. Admission must use each entry's proved maximum; redo estimates if larger. Independent arithmetic check with 6,512 input and192 output tokens reproduced the four bound/5,000/2,500 rows: GLM43/58/29, Llama34/73/36, Qwen36/69/34, Gemma65/38/19. The 2,512-input/40-output example has maximum24 across the listed rates. Nonblocking units clarification: define inRate/outRate as Neurons per token in the reservation formula, or divide the published per-million rates by1,000,000 explicitly; the table already uses that conversion. Round settled charges explicitly to the stated integer accounting unit.\n\nValidation: committed full revision delta and relevant complete sections read; native resolution/text validation and internal read/session/observation boundaries inspected; pure native-value and arithmetic probes run. Retained preflight33e29cec anticipated F2; this is the exact-head verdict. No source edits, gate rerun, live provider call, push or deployment. No approval of the real catalog, runtime or deployed journey is implied.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:32416b50eb16af2090e9fea4cc4b4952d268be60","binding":"assigned","head":"c2a938830df4534589af7f9c32d294a381b20c8c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c22fa392a887414c2c26828b70b3116d14e3238\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:30ea3552319353ce5b85ff41a824d87eb7656478\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c22fa392a887414c2c26828b70b3116d14e3238","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"cha